1
00:00:00,210 --> 00:00:02,180
At the end of Harbor's Friday, Morgan

2
00:00:02,350 --> 00:00:03,970
has a full Operating File.

3
00:00:04,220 --> 00:00:07,420
It contains a job, sources, receipts,

4
00:00:07,590 --> 00:00:09,920
authority limits, a team handoff,

5
00:00:10,070 --> 00:00:13,180
evaluation cases, a proof outline, a

6
00:00:13,230 --> 00:00:15,530
research proposal, and a six-beat

7
00:00:15,570 --> 00:00:16,140
rehearsal.

8
00:00:16,516 --> 00:00:19,716
The file is impressive in one sense: its gaps are visible.

9
00:00:20,185 --> 00:00:21,679
Staffing is still unconfirmed.

10
00:00:22,063 --> 00:00:23,087
Spend is unapproved.

11
00:00:23,556 --> 00:00:25,092
The research test has not run.

12
00:00:25,476 --> 00:00:27,097
The board proof has not been shared.

13
00:00:27,598 --> 00:00:33,572
The capstone asks whether this design deserves to continue, in what smaller form, and under whose care.

14
00:00:34,212 --> 00:00:40,740
Chapter Twenty-Six names five operating questions: route, log, gate, memory, review.

15
00:00:41,380 --> 00:00:42,318
Who receives the work?

16
00:00:42,762 --> 00:00:43,957
What record explains it?

17
00:00:44,341 --> 00:00:45,237
Where does a human decide?

18
00:00:45,877 --> 00:00:47,669
What may be remembered, and by whom?

19
00:00:48,138 --> 00:00:49,717
When will someone revisit the rule?

20
00:00:50,357 --> 00:00:55,008
The companion workbook expands these into an Accountability Stack from source through rollback.

21
00:00:55,619 --> 00:01:02,020
We will use the larger worksheet to audit the single Harbor workflow, while keeping the five questions as a readable spine.

22
00:01:02,745 --> 00:01:03,982
Begin with source and event.

23
00:01:04,409 --> 00:01:08,420
Harbor's three course inputs use opaque references and a source-status field.

24
00:01:09,034 --> 00:01:11,807
No raw private record belongs in the learner export.

25
00:01:12,362 --> 00:01:16,714
The receipt describes a paper event shape; it does not certify that an agent ran.

26
00:01:17,294 --> 00:01:24,206
Next, proposal and memory: the staffing rule and source-status rule are proposals until Morgan approves a local plan.

27
00:01:24,633 --> 00:01:26,339
A missing approval date stays blank.

28
00:01:26,766 --> 00:01:28,985
Do not backfill it to make the stack look complete.

29
00:01:29,687 --> 00:01:32,759
Move to routing, action, approval, and cost.

30
00:01:33,356 --> 00:01:35,916
The preparation role may draft a Session Option Brief.

31
00:01:36,343 --> 00:01:37,964
Morgan owns the session recommendation.

32
00:01:38,391 --> 00:01:40,012
A separate owner must review spend.

33
00:01:40,671 --> 00:01:45,578
The agent cannot book, send, buy, or turn a proposal into a team rule.

34
00:01:46,047 --> 00:01:50,015
We have no evidence that staffing is available, so the next action is still hold.

35
00:01:50,442 --> 00:01:52,746
A capstone score cannot lift that hold.

36
00:01:53,354 --> 00:01:56,640
It can identify who must decide and what evidence they need.

37
00:01:57,109 --> 00:01:58,730
Finish with export and rollback.

38
00:01:59,242 --> 00:02:02,528
The proof outline is scoped to an audience and remains `not shared`.

39
00:02:03,232 --> 00:02:08,949
If a claim is wrong, Harbor can retain the prior draft, correct the paper brief, and record the reason.

40
00:02:09,845 --> 00:02:16,416
If a local rule later causes harm, a named owner must be able to narrow, revoke, or retire it.

41
00:02:16,902 --> 00:02:22,577
The weakest gate today is staffing confirmation: without it, the brief cannot become a team proposal.

42
00:02:22,961 --> 00:02:25,435
That is a useful result, even though nothing launches.

43
00:02:25,819 --> 00:02:26,075
Pause.

44
00:02:26,886 --> 00:02:28,464
Pick the weakest gate in your workflow.

45
00:02:28,912 --> 00:02:33,178
Would you keep the design as a paper trial, shrink its scope, or retire it?

46
00:02:33,733 --> 00:02:37,232
Name the human who can make that call and the evidence that person would need.

47
00:02:37,829 --> 00:02:39,706
Use a fictional or approved example.

48
00:02:40,218 --> 00:02:42,053
Do not use private operational data.

49
00:02:42,628 --> 00:02:45,188
A blank disposition is pending, never consent.

50
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:48,303
Present your Operating File as a one-page audit.

51
00:02:48,772 --> 00:02:56,879
Walk source, event, proposal, memory, routing, action, approval, cost, export, and rollback.

52
00:02:57,401 --> 00:03:04,100
For each layer, write owner, evidence, privacy tier, gate, failure mode, and next improvement.

53
00:03:04,441 --> 00:03:05,934
Mark missing evidence openly.

54
00:03:06,532 --> 00:03:12,633
Then write a human disposition field with decision, owner, date, reason, and next review date.

55
00:03:13,285 --> 00:03:14,565
You may leave the decision pending.

56
00:03:15,162 --> 00:04:07,586
This is a design review: do not deploy, publish, spend, contact anyone, or run an agent because a worksheet is complete.

57
00:04:08,226 --> 00:04:09,890
Save revision sixteen for review.

58
00:04:10,554 --> 00:04:17,722
Morgan's safest current recommendation is to keep the paper design and shrink the next test to staffing evidence and a reviewed brief format.

59
00:04:18,262 --> 00:04:20,312
Only Morgan and the appropriate owners

60
00:04:20,442 --> 00:04:22,142
can make that disposition real.

61
00:04:22,442 --> 00:04:24,232
The file gives them a way to see what is

62
00:04:24,322 --> 00:04:26,582
ready, what is missing, and what must

63
00:04:26,712 --> 00:04:27,222
stop.
